# LTs.Soong Project Rules

These rules apply to the `LTs.Soong` repository and supplement generic guidance in `AGENTS.md`.

## Repository Identity

- Repository and solution name: `LTs.Soong`.
- Main project names use the form `LTs.Soong.<Area>`.
- Solution file: `src\LTs.Soong.slnx`.
- ReSharper solution settings: `src\LTs.Soong.sln.DotSettings`.

## Current Solution Organization

- Core project: `src\LTs.Soong.Core`
- Core unit tests: `src\LTs.Soong.Core.test`
- Core integration tests: `src\LTs.Soong.Core.test.integration`
- Host project: `src\LTs.Soong.Host`
- Host unit tests: `src\LTs.Soong.Host.test`
- LLM project: `src\LTs.Soong.LLM`
- LLM unit tests: `src\LTs.Soong.LLM.test`
- LLM integration tests: `src\LTs.Soong.LLM.test.integration`
- Learning project: `src\LTs.Soong.Learning`
- Memory project: `src\LTs.Soong.Memory`
- Skills project: `src\LTs.Soong.Skills`
- UI project: `src\LTs.Soong.UI`

## JSON

- Do not add `System.Text.Json` usage in new code in `LTs.Soong.Core`, `LTs.Soong.Host`, `LTs.Soong.Skills`, `LTs.Soong.Memory`, `LTs.Soong.Learning`, or `LTs.Soong.UI`.
- Use `LTs.Json` version `10.0.0-preview2`, aligned with other LTsoft packages in this solution.

## LLM And Ollama

- `LTs.Soong.LLM` owns provider-neutral LLM abstractions and provider implementations.
- `OllamaClient` uses `LTs.Web.HttpHandler`, not direct `HttpClient` usage.
- Unit tests for `OllamaClient` mock `HttpHandler`.
- Unit tests for `OllamaLlmClient` mock `IOllamaClient`.
- Tests that call a real local Ollama server belong in `LTs.Soong.LLM.test.integration`.
- The known local model used by integration tests is `qwen2.5-coder:14b`.

## Core

- Keep `LTs.Soong.Core` free of direct LLM provider dependencies unless explicitly requested.
- Core integration tests should exercise real Core orchestration classes together, such as `SoongAgent`, `EchoPlanner`, and `ToolRegistry`.
- Use small test-only tools inside Core integration tests when needed to avoid external dependencies.

## Host

- `LTs.Soong.Host` is the composition layer that wires Core, LLM, and tools together.
- Host-specific planners and factories belong in Host, not Core.
- Use an explicit `Program` class with `Main`, private static setup methods on `Program`, and no top-level statements.

## Style

- Order class and record members: properties, fields, constructors, methods.
- Within each member group, order by accessibility: public, protected, private.
- Do not add nested classes or records unless explicitly requested.

## Testing

- Add or update unit tests in the matching test project for every production code change in the same pass.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` testing rules, including separate Arrange/Act/Assert blocks.
- Do not duplicate production `<PackageReference>` entries in test projects; use `<ProjectReference>` and production public APIs instead.
- The expression before `.Should()` must be a local variable or parameter name only.
- Do not insert a blank line between a variable assignment and its assertion.
- Insert a blank line between separate assertion groups in the Assert block.
- Prefer combined FluentAssertions checks such as `NotBeNullOrEmpty()` instead of separate `NotBeNull()` and `NotBeEmpty()` on the same subject.
- Use `subject.Should().Be...()` and extend FluentAssertions assertion types for custom checks.

## Git And Release Notes

- When completing a set of changes, always provide the commit comment text using the format in `AGENTS.md`.
- Append commit bullet lines to `ReleaseNotes\v0.1.0.md` under `## Changes` using the LTsoft flat release notes style.
- Do not create a new release notes version file until the user explicitly starts a new version release.

## Git Commit Example

```text
1 - Add Core agent tests, integration project, and AGENTS.md.

- Add LTs.Soong.Core.test.integration with SoongAgentIntegrationTests.
- Refactor Core unit tests into SoongAgentTests with Infrastructure helpers.
- Register the integration test project in the solution.
```
